            <ArticleTitle>Comparison of in-hospital and one-year outcomes after multiple coronary arterial stenting in patients &gt; or =80 years old versus those &lt;80 years old.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>443-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The present study evaluated in-hospital and 1-year outcomes after multivessel stenting in patients aged &gt; or =80 (75 patients, 241 lesions) and &lt;80 years (894 patients, 2,678 lesions). Despite a high technical success rate of multivessel stenting, octogenarians had higher in-hospital cardiac and noncardiac complication rates and a higher mortality rate at 1-year clinical follow-up compared with their younger counterparts.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
